    <title>Past Medical History</title>
    <text><paragraph>Historical biography with true dates. These events are not part of the synthetic care timeline.</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Historical date</th><th>History</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>December 1794</td><td>One pregnancy; her only child born when she was 42</td><td>D (CLM-0003)</td></tr><tr><td>About August 1810</td><td>A small, heavy pain in the breast from about August 1810, increasing week by week, treated for months without success, with a hardening of the affected spot and her right arm kept from use; the breast was not discolored</td><td>D (CLM-0005)</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

