    <text><list><item>Invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast, multicentric (2.6 cm at 10 o&apos;clock and 0.8 cm at 7 o&apos;clock), grade 2, estrogen and progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative, pT2(m) pN0(sn) M0, anatomic stage IIA, recurrence score 13; suspected at presentation, confirmed by core biopsy four days later, and treated by right total mastectomy with sentinel node biopsy; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the documented 1811 breast disease and mastectomy, whose cancer diagnosis is debated: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

