    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Diagnostic mammography and ultrasound, then image-guided core biopsy with ER, PR, and HER2 testing, for a palpable breast mass in a woman of 59. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Breast surgery consultation to discuss surgical options, imaging of the extent of disease, axillary staging, and anesthesia and pain control. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Germline genetic testing before surgery, as recommended for breast cancer diagnosed at 65 or younger. Guideline: Germline Testing in Patients With Breast Cancer: ASCO-Society of Surgical Oncology Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2024 (2024) [S]</item><item>Right total mastectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy under general anesthesia with a pectoral nerve block and an opioid-sparing recovery pathway. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Anastrozole 1 mg daily for five years, with a baseline DXA repeated every two years, vitamin D and calcium, lipid monitoring, and questions about joint pain, hot flashes, and vaginal symptoms at every visit. Guideline: Adjuvant Endocrine Therapy for Women With Hormone Receptor-Positive Breast Cancer: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Focused Update (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Survivorship care: history and examination every 3 to 6 months for 3 years and a yearly mammogram of the left breast, with no routine blood tests or body imaging; lymphedema counseling and shoulder exercises; distress screening; a written survivorship care plan. Guideline: American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016); Breast Cancer Follow-Up and Management After Primary Treatment: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Update. J Clin Oncol 2013;31(7):961-965 (2013); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to breast surgery, Gideon Marsh, MD, ordered 2026-08-10 [S]</item></list></text>

